{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 889 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "fa485bd5a97bacd0755dbe7fc0fee848d71de097f217d0b5a88a215a1d0dba32" :edb/db-before-t 888 :edb/db-after-t 889 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534201 50 #inst "2026-10-06T10:20:14.281Z" 13194139534201 true] [17592186157062 1100 "Solve the inequality $2(x - 2)^3 - 5 \\gt      11.$" 13194139534201 true] [17592186157062 1100 "Solve the inequality $2(x - 2)^3 - 5 \\gt 11$." 13194139534201 false] [17592186157062 1145 "Isolating the cubic term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x-2)^{3}-5 & >11 \\\\ 2(x-2)^{3} & >16 \\\\ (x-2)^{3} & >8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the cube root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{(x-2)^{3}} & >\\sqrt[3]{8} \\\\ x-2 & >2 \\\\ x & >4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534201 true] [17592186157062 1145 "Isolating the cubic term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2(x - 2)^{3} - 5 & > 11 \\\\ 2(x - 2)^{3} & > 16 \\\\ (x - 2)^{3} & > 8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the cube root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt[3]{(x - 2)^{3}} & > \\sqrt[3]{8} \\\\ x - 2 & > 2 \\\\ x & > 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" 13194139534201 false] [17592186157063 1100 "Solve $(5x-1)^6 + 5 \\geq -4$." 13194139534201 false] [17592186157063 1100 "Solve $(5x-1)^6 + 5 \\geq -4.$" 13194139534201 true] [17592186157063 1145 "Isolating the sixth-degree term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5x-1)^{6}+5 & \\ge -4 \\\\ (5x-1)^{6} & \\ge -9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $(5x - 1)^{6} \\geq 0$ for all values of $x$ because the power $(6)$ is even.\n\nTherefore, the solution to the given inequality is all real numbers." 13194139534201 true] [17592186157063 1145 "Isolating the sixth-degree term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}(5x - 1)^{6} + 5 & \\ge - 4 \\\\ (5x - 1)^{6} & \\ge - 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNote that\n\n$$\n(5x - 1)^{6} \\geq 0\n$$\n\nfor all values of $x$ because the power $(6)$ is even.\n\nTherefore, the solution to the given inequality is all real numbers." 13194139534201 false] [17592186157064 1100 "Solve the inequality $\\dfrac{(5x + 2)^4}{9} - 3 \\gt 6$." 13194139534201 false] [17592186157064 1100 "Solve the inequality $\\dfrac{(5x + 2)^4}{9} - 3 \\gt 6.$" 13194139534201 true] [17592186157064 1145 "Isolating the quartic term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(5x+2)^{4}}{9}-3 & >6 \\\\ \\frac{(5x+2)^{4}}{9} & >9 \\\\ (5x+2)^{4} & >81.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take the fourth root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[4]{(5x+2)^{4}} & >\\sqrt[4]{81} \\\\ |5x+2| & >3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n5x + 2 \\lt -3 \\qquad \\textrm{or} \\qquad 5x + 2 \\gt 3\n$$\n\nWe can solve each inequality using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+2 & <-3 &  &  & 5x+2 & >3 \\\\ 5x & <-5 &  &  & 5x & >1 \\\\ x & <-1 &  &  & x & >\\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\nx \\lt -1 \\quad \\textrm{or} \\quad x \\gt \\dfrac{1}{5}.\n$$" 13194139534201 true] [17592186157064 1145 "Isolating the quartic term, we find\n$\\begin{bmatrix}((5x + 2)^{4})/(9) - 3 & > 6 \\\\ ((5x + 2)^{4})/(9) & > 9 \\\\ (5x + 2)^{4} & > 81\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nNow, we take the fourth root of both sides and get\n$\\sqrt[4]{(5x + 2)^{4}} \\mid > \\sqrt[4]{81}; \\mid 5x + 2 \\mid \\mid > 3$.\n\nThis corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n$5x + 2 \\lt -3 \\qquad \\textrm{or} \\qquad 5x + 2 \\gt 3$\n\nWe can solve each inequality using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}5x + 2 & < - 3 & 5x + 2 & > 3 \\\\ 5x & < - 5 & 5x & > 1 \\\\ x & < - 1 & x & > \\frac{1}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\nx \\lt -1 \\quad \\textrm{or} \\quad x \\gt \\dfrac{1}{5}\n$$" 13194139534201 false] [17592186157370 1020 #edb/ref 17592186281953 13194139534201 true] [17592186157370 1020 #edb/ref 17592186281959 13194139534201 true] [17592186157370 1020 #edb/ref 17592186281964 13194139534201 true] [17592186157370 1020 #edb/ref 17592186281986 13194139534201 true] [1759218615